# JOSHRIX Studio — environment.
#
# Values live in Vercel / Secret Manager, NEVER in the repo. Rotate anything that
# has ever been pasted into a chat, a prompt or a document.
#
# THIS FILE IS A CONTRACT, NOT A WISH LIST. It previously listed twenty variables
# that no code reads — BitriPay, SendGrid, Twilio, Vertex, Skybox, a JWT signing
# key — so provisioning from it meant opening accounts the platform cannot use
# while still missing PAYOUT_SECRET, without which no creator can withdraw at all.
# Every name below is read by code in this repository. If you add one, add the
# code that reads it in the same commit, or leave it out.
#
# Verify a deployment with:  curl -s https://<host>/api/health

# ============================================================================
# REQUIRED — the platform does not function without these
# ============================================================================

# Neon Postgres. The ledger, wallets, games, entitlements and payouts all live
# here. Every paid endpoint fails closed without it (ledgerRequired), which is
# deliberate: free AI is not an acceptable degradation.
DATABASE_URL=

# The ONLY admin credential. Gates /api/moderation, /api/admin-wallets,
# /api/admin-payouts. Also the fallback salt for visitor tokens if TRACK_SALT is
# unset. Never shared, never in client code.
MODERATION_KEY=

# AI providers. AT LEAST ONE is required or every forge falls through to the
# deterministic engine. The chain is tried in this order — gemini, openai,
# anthropic — and the order is measured, not preferred: the 18 Aug full-size
# probe recorded gemini complete in 39s, openai complete but only 8.4KB, and
# anthropic TRUNCATED at 159s. A deployment holding only ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is
# running on the one provider that failed the probe, with no fallback.
# /api/health reports forge.leadProvider and forge.fallbacks so you can see this.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Money in. Without these /api/topup, /api/subscribe and /api/checkout answer 503
# and nobody can buy credit, a plan, or a game.
# The webhook secret is not optional: grants are applied ONLY from the verified
# webhook, so without it a payment succeeds and the buyer receives nothing.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ============================================================================
# REQUIRED BEFORE CREATORS CAN BE PAID
# ============================================================================

# Encrypts payout destinations (AES-256-GCM, scrypt-stretched) in the ledger.
# api/_secrets.ts FAILS CLOSED: with this unset, /api/payout-destination REFUSES
# to save a bank or mobile-money destination rather than storing it in plain
# text — and wallet.html will not send a withdrawal without a saved destination.
# So an unset PAYOUT_SECRET means no creator can request a payout at all.
# Changing it later makes existing destinations unreadable; /api/admin-payouts
# warns when it cannot decrypt one.
PAYOUT_SECRET=

# ============================================================================
# RECOMMENDED — each has a documented, safe fallback, but you want these set
# ============================================================================

# Vercel Cron auth. Vercel sends `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>`. Without
# it the three scheduled jobs (blog agent, security agent, newsletter) are
# reachable by anyone who knows the path.
CRON_SECRET=

# Signs the unsubscribe token. Unset, the unsubscribe link still works but is
# unsigned — anyone could unsubscribe another person's address.
NEWSLETTER_SECRET=

# Proof-of-work challenge on account creation. UNSET = verification is OFF and
# signup falls back to rate limits alone. 18 bits is roughly 0.3-1s in a browser.
HUMAN_VERIFY_SECRET=
HUMAN_VERIFY_DIFFICULTY=18

# Salt for the daily-rotating, non-reversible visitor token. Falls back to
# MODERATION_KEY. No cookies are set and no IP is ever stored.
TRACK_SALT=

# Where /api/contact delivers. Falls back to SMTP_USER.
CONTACT_INBOX=

# ============================================================================
# EMAIL — set ONE rail. Unset, mail is sandbox-logged and never delivered.
# ============================================================================

# Rail 1 (preferred): your own domain mailbox over SMTP.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.hostinger.com
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=no-reply@joshrix.com
SMTP_PASS=

# Rail 2 (alternative): resend.com HTTP API. Used only if SMTP is not configured.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Sender shown to recipients. Defaults to SMTP_USER.
COMMS_FROM="JOSHRIX <no-reply@joshrix.com>"

# ============================================================================
# OPTIONAL — overrides with working defaults
# ============================================================================

# Model pins. Defaults: gemini-2.5-flash, gpt-4o.
GEMINI_MODEL=
OPENAI_MODEL=

# Global kill switch. FORGE_DISABLED=1 stops all paid AI endpoints and returns
# the message below. Use it during an incident rather than pulling provider keys,
# which would silently downgrade builds to the engine instead of stopping them.
FORGE_DISABLED=
FORGE_DISABLED_MESSAGE=

# Firebase project that owns user identities. A CONSTANT in shared/firebase.ts
# ("tradeconnect-tzm9l") because it is public by design and a missing env var on
# the auth path would lock every user out of their wallet. Set this ONLY to
# migrate projects, and change frontend/assets/config.js in the same commit —
# tests/t33-auth.js asserts the two match.
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=

# ============================================================================
# REPORTING ONLY — setting these changes a boolean and nothing else
# ============================================================================
# These four are read in exactly ONE place: providerStatus() in api/_gateway.ts,
# which surfaces them as booleans on /api/health. No code path calls any of these
# services. They are declared here rather than hidden in a comment because the
# code does read them — but do not buy an account expecting a feature. The
# ultra-realism pipeline in docs/REALISM-PIPELINE.md is a specification, not an
# implementation.
IMAGE_GEN_API_KEY=
MESHY_API_KEY=
TRIPO_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ============================================================================
# NOT IMPLEMENTED — do not buy accounts for these
# ============================================================================
# The names below appear in specs and in customer-facing copy, but NO code in
# this repository reads them. Setting them changes nothing at all. Listed so the
# gap is visible rather than implied, and so nobody pays for an integration that
# does not exist.
#
#   Payout execution   — /api/payout QUEUES a request; an operator moves the
#                        money by hand and marks it paid in /api/admin-payouts.
#                        There is no Stripe Connect and no BitriPay integration,
#                        despite BitriPay appearing in customer-facing copy.
#                        STRIPE_CONNECT_CLIENT_ID, BITRIPAY_API_KEY,
#                        BITRIPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#
#   Other media        — SKYBOX_API_KEY, MUSIC_GEN_API_KEY
#
#   Comms alternatives — SENDGRID_API_KEY, TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN.
#                        Email goes over SMTP or Resend; there is no SMS anywhere.
#
#   Auth / signing     — JWT_SIGNING_KEY, WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET. Identity is a
#                        Firebase ID token verified in api/_auth.ts; Stripe
#                        signs its own webhooks. Neither of these is used.
#
#   Vertex / GCP       — VERTEX_PROJECT_ID, VERTEX_LOCATION,
#                        GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS, FIREBASE_API_KEY,
#                        FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN, FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET. The
#                        client Firebase config lives in frontend/assets/config.js
#                        and is public by design.
#
#   Tax                — no automatic_tax or tax_behavior is set on any Stripe
#                        session. Selling digital goods to UK/EU consumers has
#                        VAT obligations; Stripe Tax is a configuration change on
#                        the existing account, not a new key.
#
#   Error monitoring   — there is none. No Sentry, no Datadog. /api/forge-log
#                        records forge outcomes but nothing pushes an alert.
